title RecruitBook Batch 2 — Student Profile Foundation (Use Cases)

left to right direction

' ============================================================
' ACTORS
' Only Student and Platform Administrator connect to Batch 2
' use cases. Counselor and Admissions Officer are NOT declared
' as actors here — see the "Deferred Actors / Out of Scope"
' note below instead of adding dangling actor icons.
' ============================================================

actor "Student\n(authenticated, active, owner)" as Student
actor "Platform Administrator" as PlatformAdmin

' ============================================================
' SYSTEM BOUNDARY
' ============================================================

rectangle "Batch 2: Student Profile Foundation" {

  ' ----------------------------------------------------------
  ' Profile Overview & Completion (read)
  ' Completion is DERIVED from field presence, never stored.
  ' ----------------------------------------------------------

  package "Profile Overview" as PKG_Overview {
    usecase "View Profile Overview" as UC_ViewOverview
    usecase "View Completion Indicator\n(derived, not stored)" as UC_ViewCompletion
  }

  ' ----------------------------------------------------------
  ' Profile Editing — owner only
  ' Each use case writes only the owner's own profile rows.
  ' ----------------------------------------------------------

  package "Profile Editing (Owner Only)" as PKG_Edit {
    usecase "Edit Basic Profile Information" as UC_EditBasic
    usecase "Manage Academic Background" as UC_ManageAcademic
    usecase "Manage Activities" as UC_ManageActivities
    usecase "Manage Achievements" as UC_ManageAchievements
    usecase "Edit Narrative Fields\n(plain text only)" as UC_EditNarrative
  }

  ' ----------------------------------------------------------
  ' Admin Moderation — read only
  ' No admin write path to profile content in Batch 2.
  ' ----------------------------------------------------------

  package "Admin Moderation (Read Only)" as PKG_Admin {
    usecase "Read Student Profile\n(moderation / support)" as UC_AdminRead
  }

}

' ============================================================
' ACTOR ASSOCIATIONS
' ============================================================

' --- Student (owner): full CRUD over own profile ---
' View Completion Indicator is reached via <<include>> from
' View Profile Overview, so no direct Student association here.
Student --> UC_ViewOverview
Student --> UC_EditBasic
Student --> UC_ManageAcademic
Student --> UC_ManageActivities
Student --> UC_ManageAchievements
Student --> UC_EditNarrative

' --- Platform Administrator: read-only moderation/support ---
PlatformAdmin --> UC_AdminRead

' ============================================================
' INCLUDE RELATIONSHIPS
' ============================================================

' The overview surfaces the derived completion indicator.
UC_ViewOverview ..> UC_ViewCompletion : <<include>>

' ============================================================
' NOTES
' Kept short by design — detailed policy language lives in
' comments below, not in note boxes, to keep the diagram
' readable. See diagram_rules.md STYLE-R-06.
' ============================================================

note top of Student
  Requires authenticated, active
  student owner. Ownership enforced
  server-side and by RLS.
end note

note bottom of UC_ViewCompletion
  Derived from field presence.
  Never a stored column.
end note

note bottom of UC_EditNarrative
  Plain text only.
  No markdown or rich text.
end note

note bottom of PKG_Admin
  Read-only. No admin write
  path to profile content.
end note

note as N_Deferred
  Deferred Actors / Out of Scope:
  Counselor (Batch 3 review),
  Admissions Officer (Batch 4 discovery).
  Also deferred: AI contextualization,
  profile publishing, file uploads,
  profile photos.
  No service-role usage in Batch 2.
end note

' ------------------------------------------------------------
' Extended policy language (kept out of visible note boxes):
'
' - Every Student use case requires application_users.role =
'   student and account_status = active, checked server-side
'   via the existing route guard, never trusted from the client.
' - A Student can never read or edit another Student's profile;
'   profile IDs submitted from forms are treated only as lookup
'   keys and re-validated against the owning DB row.
' - Platform Administrator access uses the existing
'   is_platform_admin() policy and is limited to read-only
'   moderation/support; there is no admin write path to profile
'   content in Batch 2 (admins moderate accounts, not profiles).
' - No stored profile status (draft/submitted/reviewed/published)
'   is introduced in Batch 2 — completion is computed, not
'   persisted, and any submission/status workflow is deferred.
' - Counselor review (Batch 3) and admissions discovery/search
'   (Batch 4) are out of scope; those actors are intentionally
'   absent from this diagram rather than shown unconnected.
' ------------------------------------------------------------

@enduml
